  "text": "AOKAННОТАНNC HABIlI\nSection 6. REPEAL. Upon the adoption of this Ordinance No. 13, Ordinance\nNo. 9, and all ordinances or resolutions or parts of ordinances or resolutions inconsistent\nwith the provisions of this ordinance are hereby repealed and replaced by this Ordinance\nNo. 13, which shall be known as and referred to as the \"Clear Creek County Traffic Code\".\nThis Ordinance does not repeal any other Clear Creek County provisions or\nenactments Allowing or regulating load and weight permits, road closures, or the use of off\nroad vehicles, all terrain vehicles, and snowmobiles on county roads.\nSection 7. CONFLICTS. Where any provision of this Ordinance conflicts with\nany other provision of this Ordinance, or any other law or ordinance, the more stringent\nrequirement, regulation, restriction or limitation shall apply.\nSection 8. CERTIFICATION. The County Clerk shall certity to the passage of\nthis Ordinance and make not less than three copies of the adopted Model Tratfic Code\navailable for inspection by the public during regular business hours.\nINTRODUCED, READ AND ORDERED PUBLISHED BY THE BOARD OF\nCOUNTY COMMISSIONERS OF CLEAR CREEK COUNTY, COLORADO, THIS\n17\"\nDAY OF\nAPRIL\n2018\nBOARD OF COUNTY COMMISSIONERS\nCLEAR CREEK\nAR CREIOUNIYCOLORADO\nTimothy J. Mauck, Chairman\nRandalí Wheelock, Commissioner\nac wal\nSean C.\nWood, Commissioner\nCERTIFICATION: THE FOREGOING ORDINANCE WAS INTRODUCED AND\nREAD ON ApHI 17\n_, 2018, BY THE BOARD OF COUNTY\nCOMMISSIONERS OF CLEAR CREEK COUNTY, COLORADO, AND APPROVED\nFOR PUBLICATION.\nDATE OF PUBLICATION: 4|25/18\negrwather\nBeth Luther\nDeputy Clerk & Recorder\nClear Creek County\nG:\\14 County Ord. & Policies\\ORDINANCESIOrdinance #13 MTCIOrd #13 New CCC MTC.Docx",
